4. Public Website

4.1 Homepage

The homepage must display:

- Website identity and logo.
- Minimal navigation.
- Search access.
- Dynamic category navigation.
- Recently published articles.
- Article thumbnails when available.
- Article titles.
- Short excerpts when useful.
- Publication dates when appropriate.
- Pagination or another crawlable article-discovery mechanism.

The homepage must automatically reflect published content from Supabase.

Do not display drafts, scheduled articles whose publication time has not arrived, or unpublished content.

Avoid unnecessary sections.

4.2 Article Detail Page

Every published article must have its own permanent, human-readable URL.

Example:

"https://gorajon.site/category-slug/article-slug"

Use a consistent URL architecture. If a category changes, avoid unnecessarily breaking existing article URLs.

Each article page must support:

- Article title.
- Article content.
- Optional featured image.
- Author attribution when configured.
- Publication date.
- Updated date when appropriate.
- Category and subcategory links.
- Proper heading hierarchy.
- Internal article links.
- Related articles when relevant.
- Breadcrumb navigation.
- Social sharing metadata.
- Article-specific SEO metadata.

Render article content safely. Sanitize any HTML that could introduce scripts or unsafe elements.

Do not expose unpublished articles through public routes.

4.3 Category Pages

Each category must have a dedicated public page.

Display:

- Category name.
- Optional category description.
- Published articles in that category.
- Article thumbnails and titles.
- Pagination when necessary.

Categories must be managed dynamically from Supabase.

Do not hardcode category names in frontend components.

4.4 Subcategory Pages

Support subcategories associated with parent categories.

Each subcategory must have its own configurable slug and public article listing.

The administrator must be able to create, edit, and delete subcategories.

4.5 Search

Implement functional article search.

Requirements:

- Search article titles and relevant content.
- Exclude unpublished articles.
- Use a search input that works on mobile and desktop.
- Provide a useful empty-results state.
- Use URL query parameters where appropriate.
- Avoid generating unlimited crawlable search-result URLs.

For a small publication, start with PostgreSQL search capabilities and add more sophisticated search only if justified.

4.6 Pagination

Implement pagination for article listings.

Requirements:

- Stable page URLs.
- Correct previous and next navigation.
- No duplicated articles between pages.
- Appropriate SEO metadata and canonical URLs.
- Avoid infinite-scroll-only navigation.

4.7 Essential Static Pages

Create simple, manageable pages for:

- About.
- Contact.
- Privacy Policy.
- Terms and Conditions.
- Disclaimer.

These pages should contain editable content where appropriate.

Do not fabricate business addresses, legal identities, or contact details. Use clearly marked placeholders until the administrator supplies accurate information.

